<page xmlns="http://projectmallard.org/1.0/"
      type="topic"
      id="vendor_payment">

  <info>
  <link type="guide" xref="vendor"/>
  <link type="seealso" xref="unprocessed_po"/>
  <link type="seealso" xref="incoming_invoice"/>
  <desc>Pay vendors' invoices by check, debit, cash or credit card.</desc>
    <credit type="author">
      <name>Reuben Rissler</name>
      <email>pygtk.posting@gmail.com</email>
    </credit>
  </info>

  <title>Vendor payment</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Vendor</gui><gui>Vendor payment</gui></guiseq>, or the
  <gui>Vendor Payment</gui> button of the main window, pays the vendor
  invoices saved in <link xref="unprocessed_po"/>. <gui>Save and pay
  ...</gui> there opens it with the bill just saved already chosen.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Vendor</gui>, or check <gui>View all</gui> to
    list every vendor's unpaid invoices.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check the <gui>Date</gui> of the payment.</p></item>
    <item><p>Select the invoices to pay. Hold <key>Ctrl</key> to select
    several and pay them together.</p></item>
    <item><p>Pay on one of the two tabs below, as described next.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <section id="check">
  <title>Pay with check / debit</title>
  <p>Choose the bank account under <gui>from bank account</gui>. Then
  either:</p>
  <list>
    <item><p>Type the <gui>Check number</gui> and click <gui>Print
    check</gui>. The check prints on your check form and the payment is
    posted. As with an invoice, checking <gui>Cancel printing and
    posting</gui> in the print dialog stops both. <gui>Post check without
    printing</gui> posts a check written by hand.</p></item>
    <item><p>For a bank debit or transfer, type the <gui>Transaction
    number</gui> and click <gui>Debit</gui>.</p></item>
  </list>
  </section>

  <section id="cash_card">
  <title>Pay with cash / credit card</title>
  <p>The <gui>Description</gui> is what the payment is called on the credit
  card statement; it starts as the invoice's name.</p>
  <list>
    <item><p>To pay cash, choose the account <gui>from cash account</gui>
    and click <gui>Pay</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>To pay by card, choose the card <gui>from credit card</gui> and
    click its <gui>Pay</gui>. A payment can be split into several card
    charges on different dates: the add and delete buttons beside the list
    (<gui>Add split payment entry</gui>, <gui>Remove split payment
    entry</gui>) add and remove charges, and you type each one's amount and
    date. The charges must add up to the invoices selected.</p></item>
  </list>
  <p>Each <gui>Pay</gui> button says what is missing until it can be used,
  for instance <gui>No invoice selected</gui> or <gui>Invoice and payment do
  not match</gui>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="right_click">
  <title>Right click an invoice</title>
  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>View attachment</gui></title>
    <p>Opens the scan of the vendor's invoice, if one was attached.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Correct purchase order</gui></title>
    <p>Opens the order to correct what was invoiced; see <link
    xref="unprocessed_po#correct"/>.</p></item>
  </terms>
  </section>

</page>
